<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"><title><%= title %> - EliteHackLab</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css"></head>
<body>
  <div class="matrix-bg"></div>
  <nav class="main-nav"><div class="nav-brand"><span class="brand-icon">💀</span><span class="brand-text">Elite<span class="highlight">Hack</span>Lab</span></div><div class="nav-links"><a href="/"><i class="fas fa-home"></i> Dashboard</a></div></nav>
  <div class="lab-container">
    <div class="lab-header"><h1>⚡ Race Condition Labs</h1></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-book"></i> Theory</h2><p>Race conditions exploit the time gap between a security check and the use of that check (TOCTOU). By sending many simultaneous requests, attackers can bypass limits, double-spend, or reuse tokens.</p>
    <div class="code-block">// Vulnerable pattern:
if (balance >= amount) {   // CHECK
  // ... window for race ...
  balance -= amount;        // USE
}

// Attack: Send 10 concurrent requests to withdraw $1000 each
// If balance is $1000, you might withdraw $10000!</div></div>
    <div class="lab-section"><h2><i class="fas fa-flask"></i> Labs</h2><div class="lab-list"><% labs.forEach(function(lab) { %><a href="<%= lab.path %>" class="lab-link"><span class="lab-name"><i class="fas fa-terminal"></i> <%= lab.name %></span><span class="lab-difficulty <%= lab.difficulty.toLowerCase() %>"><%= lab.difficulty %></span></a><% }); %></div></div>
    <div style="margin-top:1rem;"><button onclick="resetLabs()" class="btn btn-danger">Reset All Race Labs</button></div>
  </div>
  <script src="/js/main.js"></script>
  <script>async function resetLabs(){const r=await fetch('/labs/race-condition/reset',{method:'POST'});alert(JSON.stringify(await r.json()));}</script>
</body>
</html>
